{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor consistently treated the case as a high-acuity inpatient/ICU-to-ward transition rather than routine discharge, repeatedly emphasizing persistent coma, seizure recurrence risk, oxygen/airway risks, NPO status, inpatient medication control, pending results, and responsible clinician follow-up. All responsibility-chain duties were met, including concrete same-day/round checklists, escalation triggers, medication/NPO boundaries, tube/nursing boundaries, and repeated caregiver receipt. The trajectory also completed multiple high-order tasks: it dynamically reprioritized as new ICU, cardiac, nasogastric, rehab, and discharge-transition issues surfaced; verified ambiguous family-reported data; created safe bounded closure; and navigated family coordination barriers. With no responsibility-chain error or important non-chain defect and at least two completed high-order points with meaningful impact, the deterministic grade is Perfect.",
